# factory-dashboard — the feed's private settings (copy to .env, chmod 600; .env is gitignored).
#
# Every build, planning, approval and delivery fact comes from Forge's record, mounted read-only
# (design of 17 October 2026), so the feed needs no NATS login.
#
# LiteLLM refuses an unauthenticated `GET /v1/models` (401). The feed's health check (every 30 s,
# models list only, no model calls) sends this dashboard-only LiteLLM key to LiteLLM and nowhere
# else. Mint it with the LiteLLM master key (alias factory-dashboard-…); leave it empty and the
# check is refused.
FACTORY_LITELLM_KEY=

# The chat's own LiteLLM key (design requirement 9), limited to the `dashboard-chat` model name, so
# the chat's model use is tagged and counted on its own. Only the board receives it (compose passes
# this one value). Leave it empty and the chat says it is not switched on.
FACTORY_DASH_CHAT_KEY=

# Voice (design requirement 10): the speech-to-text and text-to-speech models behind the estate's
# llama-swap. No key. Leave these empty for the defaults shown; set them when the models move machines.
# FACTORY_DASH_STT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9000/v1/audio/transcriptions
# FACTORY_DASH_STT_MODEL=parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3
# FACTORY_DASH_TTS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9000/v1/audio/speech
# FACTORY_DASH_TTS_MODEL=qwen3-tts-0.6b
# FACTORY_DASH_TTS_VOICE=Ryan
# The longest each speech model may take over one reply, in seconds.
# FACTORY_DASH_VOICE_TIMEOUT=30
# At most this many words of an answer are read aloud (the speech model stops at about 60 seconds).
# FACTORY_DASH_SPOKEN_WORDS=45

# Answering the factory's cards from the dashboard (19 October 2026). Only the board uses it: it
# connects for each answer as the dashboard_approve user, which may only post card answers. Its
# password is NOT here: it is the file dashboard_approve_nats_password in the board's config folder.
# Leave this empty and the cards show without buttons.
# FACTORY_DASH_NATS_URL=nats://127.0.0.1:4222
